  "result": "Perfect! All 156 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/payments.js** \u2014 Payment recording and balance tracking:\n\n**`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates amount still owed:\n- Returns `invoice.total - sum(payments)`\n- Clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n**`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records payment on an invoice:\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to `invoice.payments` array\n- Creates payments array if missing\n- Updates status based on payment progress:\n  - `'paid'` when total payments >= invoice total\n  - `'partially_paid'` when payments > 0 and < total\n- Validates:\n  - `NOT_ISSUED` unless status is `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'`\n  - `AMOUNT_INVALID` unless amount is a positive integer\n  - `DATE_INVALID` unless date is YYYY-MM-DD format\n  - `OVERPAYMENT` if payment exceeds balance due\n- Preserves invoice number and all other fields\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: Only issued or partially paid invoices can receive payments\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment is more than the amount due\n\n**Tests** \u2014 21 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Balance due calculations (unpaid, partially paid, fully paid)\n- Payment recording (single and multiple payments)\n- Status transitions (draft\u2192issued\u2192partially_paid\u2192paid)\n- Validation (amount, date, invoice status, overpayment)\n- Edge cases (exact payments, accumulation, payment after partial)\n- Data integrity (no mutation, number preservation)\n- Rejection of payments on draft/paid invoices\n\nAll 156 tests pass \u2713",
